D3D12: a barrier side {MICROMAP_WRITE, MICROMAP} gets no EMIT_POSTBUILD_INFO sync.

GetBarrierSyncFlags adds D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_EMIT_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_POSTBUILD_INFO to
the ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE | MICROMAP stages unless the access holds ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_WRITE,
while GetBarrierAccessFlags maps MICROMAP_WRITE to the same
D3D12_BARRIER_ACCESS_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_WRITE. The debug layer refuses that pair and
the command list fails to close. Since 022f7e6.

This treats MICROMAP_WRITE as the write it maps to.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA, Agility 1.619: after CmdBuildMicromaps, a buffer barrier whose before side
is {MICROMAP_WRITE, MICROMAP} gave "[1331] ID3D12CommandList::Barrier: SyncBefore bits
D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_EMIT_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_POSTBUILD_INFO are incompatible with
AccessBefore bits D3D12_BARRIER_ACCESS_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_WRITE in buffer barrier at
group [0], index [0]." and Close failed with E_INVALIDARG, with the debug layer on or off; the same
barrier with ALL stages closed. With the change the micromap, committed, placed, cloned or
compacted, links into a BLAS and decides the ray query (transparent hides the triangle, opaque shows
it) with the MICROMAP stage.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
index 986537a..ca36a03 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
@@ -138,8 +138,8 @@ static inline D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC GetBarrierSyncFlags(StageBits stageBits, Access
         flags |= D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_BUILD_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE | D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_COPY_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE;
 
         // There is no "EMIT_POSTBUILD_INFO" flag in VK, moreover "VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_2_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_BUILD_BIT_KHR" already includes "ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_COPY".
-        // "EMIT_POSTBUILD_INFO" can't be set if "write" access is expected.
-        if (!(accessBits & AccessBits::ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_WRITE))
+        // "EMIT_POSTBUILD_INFO" can't be set if "write" access is expected ("MICROMAP_WRITE" is the same D3D12 write access).
+        if (!(accessBits & (AccessBits::ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_WRITE | AccessBits::MICROMAP_WRITE)))
             flags |= D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_EMIT_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_POSTBUILD_INFO;
     }
 
